cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PACK3D, please cite the paper below."
title: "PACK3D: Geometry Matters in Packed 3D Attention"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/amilworks/Pack3D"
url: "https://amilworks.github.io/Pack3D/"
abstract: >-
  PACK3D is a local-global attention operator for packed 3D token fields that separates memory
  layout from attention geometry. It attends exactly within a coordinate-defined neighborhood,
  sees the whole field through pooled summaries, and rotates queries and keys with axial RoPE at
  token-grid coordinates. The operator is equivariant to any repacking that carries coordinates,
  neighborhoods, summary memberships, and within-block slots along with the tokens.
keywords:
  - attention
  - rotary position embedding
  - 3D
  - packed sequences
  - volumetric segmentation
  - microscopy
